    "created_at": "2018-01-23T23:22:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-01-23T23:23:03Z",
    "body": "I think it is supposed to be equivalent. I don't think it's necessarily clearer to _replace_ \"return to caller\", although supplementing it might be good.\r\n\r\nThe issue is that \"spin the event loop\" is more of a spec-macro than a series of steps that you can just sub in. In its essentials, it turns:\r\n\r\n1. Do stuff 1\r\n2. Go in parallel\r\n   1. Wait a bit\r\n   2. Queue a task to do stuff 2\r\n\r\ninto\r\n\r\n1. Do stuff 1\r\n2. Spin the event loop\r\n3. Do stuff 2\r\n\r\nMaybe calling out this equivalence (similar to https://tc39.github.io/ecma262/#sec-returnifabrupt) would be helpful.\r\n\r\nBut anyway, I think \"return to the caller\" is trying to get at that equivalence, and just saying \"continue _task_\" kind of makes it less clear, because it relies on the non-obvious fact that the calling algorithm is ~ _task_.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
