    "body": "Given #4437 and #4439 in part the question is to what extent this is a real thing that can be observed. Apart from the navigate to a fragment case which can be rewritten, the hard parts are all around the HTML/XML parser. (Assuming we can adjust pausing somehow to not rely on this.)\r\n\r\n(If it is a real thing that can happen when you invoke X, X would be a rather interesting primitive as, e.g., it means a JavaScript Job can be paused while the remainder of the Job Queue gets processed.)",
